    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d894">

                <pb facs="0833" n="821" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg821"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39) Korsholm/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-05T14:00:00-05:00">October 5, 1939—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>639. Department is advised that Swedish M/S <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Korsholm</hi>, also Estonian SS <hi rendition="#italic">Minna</hi> and
                    Norwegian SS <hi rendition="#italic">Brott</hi>,<anchor n="92" xml:id="d894-f1"
                    /> each with a cargo of wood pulp or wood pulp products, consigned to various
                    concerns in the United States, have been detained at Swinemünde, Kiel, and
                    Sivinemünde, respectively.</p>
                <p>In the general interest of American commerce, ascertain the reasons for such
                    detentions and what action German authorities contemplate taking with reference
                    to the cargoes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d894-f1" n="92" xml:id="d894-f1-content">
                <p>By telegram No. 1658, October 10, 5 p.m., the Chargé in Germany reported that the
                    steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Brott</hi> and cargo had been released
                    (300.115(39)Korsholm/9).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
